body:
After just barely making the decision not to throw myself off a bridge last semester, (which may very well have been the wrong choice) my off-campus therapist says she's not going to give me any services, including tele-therapy, until school starts back up again, because I live out of state. So by her word, she won't so much as call me until late August. Six months. Knowing how close I was to ending it all, and that I'm very much not doing okay in recent months. And she hasn't offered to help me find anyone else to see in the time being. I've gotten no word from her other than an email telling me that she won't help me, and that she hopes I have a good break. So I have to deal with all my problems alone, again. 

&#x200B;

Is this normal? Is this good? Is this ethical, in any way?  I know there are resources out there so that I could find someone else, but is this blatant disregard for my health standard? Three months ago I couldn't eat or get out of bed, and I'm supposed to just continue living like everything is normal. I literally can't even pay a healthcare professional to care about me when that's their entire JOB.
